{%- comment -%}
  ORI pre-order state
  ===================
  Outputs 'pre' when a variant is being sold past zero stock, and nothing at
  all otherwise. Capture it:

    {%- capture ori_preorder -%}
      {%- render 'ori-preorder-state', product: product, variant: some_variant -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign ori_preorder = ori_preorder | strip -%}

  Scope, as of 23 Aug 2026
  ------------------------
  One caller: snippets/product-inventory.liquid, which uses it to keep the
  stock line off pre-orders. It no longer touches the buy buttons. It used to,
  and that was reverted at the client's request, because hiding the Selleasy
  "Make it a complete Kit" add-ons alongside the second button cost them the
  upsell. If you are reintroducing anything here, that is the constraint to
  design around: the add-ons have to stay on the page.

  Why this exists rather than reading variant.available
  -----------------------------------------------------
  With "Sell when out of stock" on (inventory_policy 'continue') Shopify keeps
  reporting a variant as available no matter how far past zero it goes, so
  .available cannot answer "has this run out" and the stock line would promise
  "In stock, ready to ship" with an empty shelf.

  quantity_rule_soldout is not reusable for this: it switches itself off under
  'continue', which is the exact case we care about.

  All three conditions matter:

  - inventory_management == 'shopify'. Untracked variants have a meaningless
    quantity, so they are never pre-order.
  - inventory_quantity <= 0. There is nothing on the shelf.
  - inventory_policy == 'continue'. This is the one that separates a pre-order
    from a plain sell out. "Sell when out of stock" being on is the merchant
    saying orders past zero are still wanted. With 'deny' at zero Shopify
    refuses the add anyway, so the product is simply sold out and must keep
    saying so. Timesact draws the same line: its isVariantOutOfStock() returns
    true for DENY at zero.

  Note on Timesact
  ----------------
  Timesact does NOT create Shopify selling plans. Checked on live against
  ori-electric-steps-chevy-silverado-zr2-ltz-2023, where the app reports the
  variant as ACTIVE while selling_plan_groups is []. So any check of the form
  "product.selling_plan_groups.size > 0" will never fire on this shop and is
  not a way to detect a Timesact pre-order. The quantity rule above is.

  Deliberately NOT covered here:

  - Tag driven pre-order and special order. Those are the existing ORI flow and
    open an enquiry modal instead of taking money, so they stay on their own
    so_type path. This is only about stock running out.

  Anything unexpected has to land on "sell it as normal", never on "hide it".
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign v = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign state = ''

  if v and v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and v.inventory_quantity <= 0 and v.inventory_policy == 'continue'
    assign state = 'pre'
  endif

  echo state
-%}
